hey guys it's fresh and clean vadim for  max tech and as you know  apple's wwdc just happened and they've  left us with a ton of new features and  changes  with the new ios 15 update which  surprisingly is going to be available on  iphones as old as the iphone 6s  so what i'm gonna do in this video is  weed out all of the changes  that aren't that big of a deal and just  focus on the best features and changes  that'll actually make your life better  on a daily basis  so let's get started with the first new  feature which is the newly redesigned  notification center  with changes that people have been  asking for for years  we've now got contact photos for  messages and contacts within your  notifications  as well as larger icons for apps to make  them easier to see  there's also the new notification  summary which you can schedule to get  delivered to you  at whatever time you choose and it uses  machine learning and your past activity  to put the most relevant and important  notifications at the top  and the least important at the bottom  this is going to be really awesome for  those notifications that come throughout  the day  but aren't urgent like a text message  which will always show up  instantly like a regular notification  and of course you can enable do not  disturb if you're busy  and one big change this year is that  someone else using imessage  will be able to see that you've silenced  your notifications  before they text you and if it's an  emergency  they can push it through by tapping  notify anyway  apple is taking it even further with  their new focus modes  like personal work sleep or a custom  focus  if you want to make one like for example  doing your homework  this is going to allow only the  notifications related to each focus  group to come through  so you won't get distracted with work  related notifications  while you're with your family at home  and you can even customize the apps and  people that are allowed to give you  notifications  while you're in each focus group and  even better it works across  all of your icloud devices so you can  easily turn it on using your apple watch  if that's more convenient for you moving  on the next awesome feature is  all of the huge changes made to facetime  the biggest deal  is that facetime is now finally opened  up to non-apple users  so you can create a scheduled meeting  and share a link with others so they can  join in  no matter which device they're on so  basically apple is putting zoom out of  business  because all of this is going to be  completely free and everything will have  end-to-end encryption that you can trust  on top of that one huge surprise is the  new portrait mode feature which is  supported on iphone  ipad or m1 max so the background is  going to be blurred out  so your friends and family can focus on  your face and i've got to say  this is basically hinting at apple  bringing portrait mode video to the  iphone  hopefully as soon as the iphone 13 since  that was already in the rumor mill  on top of that audio is getting improved  with both a new voice isolation feature  which gets rid of background noise and  then a wide spectrum mode  which makes background noise louder  which could potentially be useful in  some scenarios  another cool feature is share play which  allows you to share content like music  or movies with your friends  as you facetime them you can even watch  a movie together  at the same time since it syncs between  both of you  which is honestly really impressive and  since apple opened up the shareplay api  with other developers  it might be coming to apps like youtube  so you can share and show videos  with your friends but my personal  favorite part of shareplay  is that you can share your screen with  someone who needs help  with finding a setting or anything else  on their phone now moving on to the next  major change  the wallet app is now finally gonna  support various keys and badges  using the new ultra wide band chip which  is already packed into every iphone 11  and iphone 12.  for example some new cars are getting  support for apple's car key feature  so you'll be able to walk up to your car  and unlock it with just your phone  and apple is basically working on  bringing every sort of key to the wallet  app  like your house keys with specific  third-party locks  your hotel room using your iphone or  apple watch  and even your workplace if your company  supports it but apple isn't stopping  there they're allowing you to scan your  id or driver's license right into the  wallet app  so you don't have to worry about  carrying it around and apparently apple  is already working with the tsa at  airports  to get iphone identification support  this is basically ushering in  the future where we no longer need to  carry everything around with us  and i wouldn't be surprised if apple is  going to be bringing passport ids  onto iphones very soon the next great  feature that is really going to help  with  everyday life has to do with the airpods  first up there's the conversation boost  feature for airpods pro  which will amplify the voice of someone  you're talking to  and allow you to dial down the ambient  noise at the same time  which is going to be perfect for people  who require hearing aids  on top of that siri can now  automatically read your notifications to  you  and she can even read your shopping list  to you as your shopping  which is really convenient now one of  the worst things about airpods was that  they were pretty easy to lose  but now the same find my features that  came to the air tags  are now on the airpods so they can be  located by other apple devices  as people walk by them and now you can  even play  a sound to them even while they're in  the case  and use the new proximity feature to  find them but the best part of all is  the new separation  alert feature which will let you know  when you accidentally dropped your  earpods and left them behind somewhere  now moving on to the next one siri is  finally getting a new feature that i  personally wanted for years  and that's offline mode now you no  longer have to be connected to the  internet to use siri  so let's say you're out camping and you  have no service  and you simply want to set a timer you  can now finally do it with  no internet service and the reason apple  is able to do this because with the new  update  the audio never leaves your iphone  everything is processed  on device using the neural engine which  gives you a couple of advantages  it's now much more secure and private  and on top of that  siri is much faster than before since  everything is processed  on device and all of that is part of  apple's continued push for privacy  so let's get into the new privacy  features which help keep your data  safe and secure each and every day  apple's new mail privacy protection  gives you some amazing features for free  like hiding your ip address hiding your  location  and even disabling read receipts so  newsletters and advertisers  won't be able to tell if you opened an  email or not on top of that when you're  browsing the web with safari  apple automatically hides your ip  address from trackers  and you now get a new app privacy report  which will tell you the various ways  apps access your private data like your  photos webcam  contacts microphone and more within the  last seven days  even better you'll be able to see the  third-party domains that the app is  contacting  and giving your data to which is  basically facebook's  worst nightmare so it's gonna be  interesting to see how they respond  but the absolute bombshell feature that  blew my mind  is apple's new private relay feature for  people who pay for icloud plus  your internet browsing traffic gets  relayed twice so that no one  including apple can see all of your  browsing data  which basically means that it's a  reliable vpn  built into safari which is huge because  you don't have to pay  for any third-party service and on top  of that apple also has a new hide my  email feature  which lets you create single use email  addresses  that automatically forward to your  actual email account  just in case companies start sending you  a bunch of spam  and if that does end up happening you  can simply disable that specific burner  email address  and not have to worry about it now on  top of those privacy features  safari is getting some major updates  like a new redesign  with the focus on tab management with  new tab groups that you can customize  there's a new tab bar on the bottom of  the page that allows you to swipe  between the tab groups and swipe up to  reveal all the taps  there's also a new customizable start  page which automatically syncs with the  mac as well  and i think one of the most important  new features is web extensions  finally coming to the iphone and ipad so  now extensions like honey or something  else  will not be limited to just the mac and  to make it even better  extensions share code with existing  safari  extensions on the mac so it's going to  be incredibly quick and easy  for developers to bring them over to the  iphone and ipad and finally  there's a feature that i've been waiting  for for years and that's automatic  translation  you can now simply open up the translate  app and have a conversation with someone  else  both in your own native languages and  it'll automatically translate everything  for you on the fly  and on top of that you have system-wide  translation  so you can select text anywhere you see  it and tap  translate but perhaps the coolest  feature of all is able to translate text  within a  photo that you take which is useful for  when you're going on vacations to  foreign places  and that works by using apple's new live  text feature  which allows you to take photos of text  and then select it  which can be super convenient so there  you guys go those are all of the new ios  15 features that actually matter in the  real world  for everyday life so if you enjoyed this  video go ahead and click the circle  above because we've got a whole lot more  videos coming soon  definitely check out one of those two  right there thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next video  you
 

